I think there have been several misunderstandings here: what lrusak wanted is clang-format of new code lines only:

e.g:

```c++
    // EAC3 can have a dependent stream too
    if (!wantEAC3dependent)
    {
      unsigned int fsizeMain = m_fsize;
      unsigned int reqBytes = fsizeMain + 8;
      if (size < reqBytes)
      {
        // not enough data to check for E-AC3 dependent frame, request more
        m_needBytes = reqBytes;
        m_fsize = 0;
        // no need to resync => return true
        return true;
      }
      if (TrySyncAC3(data + fsizeMain, size - fsizeMain, resyncing, /*wantEAC3dependent*/ true))
      {
        // concatenate the main and dependent frames
        m_fsize += fsizeMain;
        return true;
      }
    }
```

Note that Jenkins checks formatting of each commit separately so a commit with wrong format + patch to fix format on a separated commit does not fix all Jenkins complains. Also for backport is need cherry pick same commit (if possible) so is much more easy one commit only.

@popcornmix, please update the PR with a single commit of the new code (without touching the rest of the existing code).

